    <GaugingStation location="Egleton" name="Egleton Brook" number="31026">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V weir measuring inflows to Rutland Water reservoir from a small, rural, natural catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Theoretically rated, but could drown at high flows due to sharp bend d/s and weed growth. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V weir 2m wide measuring inflows to Rutland Water.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2024 (WINFAP Files v13).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural to within 10% at Q95. No abstractions or returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Small catchment on Boulder Clay and low permeability geology. Rural, mixed farming.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
